---
<Base title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
    <section class="hero">
        <h1>Pricing</h1>
        <br>
        <div class="note pricing-free-note">
            <p>
                <strong>Heads up: the prices on this page are for businesses and enterprise users.</strong><br>
                Osprey is, and will always be completely free for home users. The pricing on this page is only for the
                Management Console used by businesses, MSPs, and IT teams.
                <br><br>If you just want to download the extension for your browser, click the button below.
            </p>
            <br>
            <a class="btn" href="/download/">Download Osprey</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
        <h2 class="band-title">What is the Management Console?</h2>
        <div class="prose">
            <p class="band-sub">
                The <a class="contact-link" href="https://console.osprey.ac">Osprey Management Console</a> is how an
                MSP or IT team runs Osprey across a whole fleet from one place. The console allows teams to enroll
                devices with a script, push policies to every browser, and see detections, offline devices, and unblock
                requests across every client or site they manage on one dashboard, with reports, alerts, and
                integrations that fit into the tools you already run. Every enrolled device gets the same full
                protection as the free extension; the console adds the management and compliance around it.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
        <h2 class="band-title">What each plan includes</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="What each plan includes">
            <table class="compare">
                <caption class="sr-only">Feature availability across the Free, Starter, Professional, and Enterprise
                    plans
                </caption>
                <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Feature</span></th>
                    <th scope="col">Free</th>
                    <th scope="col">Starter</th>
                    <th scope="col">Professional</th>
                    <th scope="col">Enterprise</th>
                </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                {
                    features.map((row) => (
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">{row.feature}</th>
                                <td>
                                    <Fragment set:html={cell(row.free)}/>
                                </td>
                                <td>
                                    <Fragment set:html={cell(row.starter)}/>
                                </td>
                                <td>
                                    <Fragment set:html={cell(row.professional)}/>
                                </td>
                                <td>
                                    <Fragment set:html={cell(row.enterprise)}/>
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                    ))
                }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
        <h2 class="band-title">How much they cost</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Plan pricing">
            <table class="compare">
                <caption class="sr-only">Pricing for the Free extension and the Starter, Professional, and Enterprise
                    Management Console plans
                </caption>
                <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Item</span></th>
                    <th scope="col">Free</th>
                    <th scope="col">Starter</th>
                    <th scope="col">Professional</th>
                    <th scope="col">Enterprise</th>
                </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                {
                    rates.map((row) => (
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="row">{row.row}</th>
                                <td><span class="val">{row.free}</span></td>
                                <td><span class="val">{row.starter}</span></td>
                                <td><span class="val">{row.professional}</span></td>
                                <td><span class="val">{row.enterprise}</span></td>
                            </tr>
                    ))
                }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <br>
        <br>
        <div class="prose">
            <p class="band-sub">
                Each period bills the highest nightly count of active seats, raised to the plan's minimum when the
                count falls below it. Seats above the minimum bill at the plan's flat per-seat rate, so the total
                always scales with the fleet. Plans can be changed self-service in either direction and take effect
                at the next period boundary. Osprey Project LLC gives 10% of its net revenue to
                the <a class="contact-link" href="https://sccf.org/">Sanibel-Captiva Conservation Foundation</a> to
                protect ospreys and their habitats. You can
                view <a class="contact-link" href="/giving/">Our Giving Pledge</a> for more information.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
        <h2 class="band-title">Questions, or ready to start?</h2>
        <div class="prose">
            <p class="band-sub">
                <a href="/contact/" class="contact-link" aria-label="Send us a message">Send us a message</a> and
                we'll set up a demo for your organization.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</Base>
